[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a classic real analysis question. The answer is YES — the Cantor [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfunction (devil's staircase) is a continuous function that maps the Cantor set [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(measure zero) to [0,1] (measure 1).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write a complete proof.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe Cantor set C has Lebesgue measure 0. The Cantor function f: [0,1] → [0,1] is[0m[38;2;124;124;124mcontinuous, and f(C) = [0,1], which has measure 1 > 0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write the proof carefully.[0m

